# =============================================================================
# Meta Marketing API
#
#   cp .env.example .env && chmod 600 .env
#
# .env is gitignored. Never commit real values, and never paste them into a
# commit message, a log line or an issue.
#
# Optional keys below are spelled out with EMPTY values on purpose, so this
# file documents everything that can be configured. That is safe here because
# every setting is read through metaads_reporting.config.env(), which treats
# "present but blank" exactly like "absent" and falls back to the code default.
# =============================================================================

# --- Required: the access token ----------------------------------------------
# USE A SYSTEM USER TOKEN, not a personal one. This is the single most
# important line in this file.
#
#   Business Settings > Users > System Users > Add
#     > Assign Assets: the ad account, with Manage Campaigns (or View
#       Performance only, if you are installing read-only)
#     > Generate New Token > pick your app > select the scopes below
#
# A personal user token dies the moment that person changes their Facebook
# password -- error code 190, subcode 460 -- and the only symptom is every call
# failing at once, at 3am, with a message about a password nobody connected to
# this. A System User has no password to change.
#
# Scopes: ads_read is enough to run reports. ads_management is required for any
# preview_*/apply_* pair to work. business_management lets /me/adaccounts list
# what the System User can reach.
#
# TWO HALVES, BOTH REQUIRED. The token needs the scope AND the System User must
# be assigned to the ad account in Business Settings. Either one alone produces
# exactly the same "permission denied", so check both before debugging either.
META_ADS_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# --- Required-ish: the ad account to work on ---------------------------------
# With or without the `act_` prefix; it is stripped and re-added as needed.
# Leave blank to be forced to pass --account-id explicitly on every command.
# Find it in the Ads Manager URL (`act=...`), or run:
#   ./.venv/bin/python scripts/fetch_report.py accounts
META_ADS_ACCOUNT_ID=

# --- Optional: app secret, for appsecret_proof -------------------------------
# Worth setting. With it, every request carries an HMAC of the token keyed by
# this secret, so a stolen token on its own is not enough to call the API. The
# secret never leaves this machine.
# App Dashboard > Settings > Basic > App Secret.
META_ADS_APP_SECRET=

# --- Optional: the business, for diagnostics ---------------------------------
# Only used to make rate-limit headers readable: Meta keys the
# X-Business-Use-Case-Usage header by business id.
META_ADS_BUSINESS_ID=

# --- Optional: overrides (blank = use the code default) ----------------------
# Graph API version. Default: see DEFAULT_API_VERSION in
# metaads_reporting/config.py.
#
# PIN THIS DELIBERATELY. An unversioned Graph request is served by the OLDEST
# version still supported, so leaving it off does not mean "latest" -- it means
# "whatever is about to be switched off". Meta ships roughly three versions a
# year and supports each for about two.
#
# Accepts "v23.0" or "23.0". After changing it, run:
#   ./.venv/bin/python scripts/test_connection.py
# which reports the version that actually answered.
META_ADS_API_VERSION=
# Graph API base URL. Only change this to point at a proxy.
META_ADS_GRAPH_BASE=
# Where exported reports are written. Default: output/ (gitignored).
META_ADS_OUTPUT_DIR=
